1
00:00:00,650 --> 00:00:05,520
This is QuietRelay, a local policy workbench for
Nostr relay operators.

2
00:00:05,620 --> 00:00:08,076
A valid signature is only the beginning.

3
00:00:08,176 --> 00:00:14,914
This note is genuinely signed, but its tags
expose a location, a relationship and a relay destination.

4
00:00:15,014 --> 00:00:19,405
These are public synthetic fixtures, not
anyone's private messages.

5
00:00:22,651 --> 00:00:24,766
Here is the exact signed event.

6
00:00:24,866 --> 00:00:27,806
The input and its signature never change.

7
00:00:27,906 --> 00:00:30,877
Under the Open policy, the note is admitted.

8
00:00:30,977 --> 00:00:33,740
Switch back to Quiet, and it is held.

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:36,200
It never enters the subscriber feed.

10
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:41,081
We are changing a visible policy, not rewriting
evidence to force a result.

11
00:00:44,153 --> 00:00:50,792
The policy diff replays all twenty fixture events
independently under each preset, from an empty store.

12
00:00:50,892 --> 00:00:54,682
Quiet admits eleven, Open fifteen, Strict five.

13
00:00:54,782 --> 00:01:02,675
Limits on kinds, tags, age, bytes and arrival rate are
explicit, so an authentic message can still fall outside the contract.

14
00:01:05,652 --> 00:01:07,375
Now a new experiment.

15
00:01:07,475 --> 00:01:15,825
Signing uses real BIP-340 Schnorr signatures, with deliberately
public demo identities that must never become real accounts.

16
00:01:15,925 --> 00:01:19,361
I ask the workbench to change the content after
signing.

17
00:01:19,461 --> 00:01:26,078
The canonical event hash no longer matches the id, so
the integrity check fails before any policy can admit it.

18
00:01:29,154 --> 00:01:30,782
Next, the real wire.

19
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:33,704
In a terminal, I start the loopback relay.

20
00:01:33,804 --> 00:01:38,388
It listens only on the local machine, and never
contacts an upstream relay.

21
00:01:41,655 --> 00:01:45,254
Back in the browser, I restore the fixtures and
run the live test.

22
00:01:45,354 --> 00:01:52,616
These are frames captured from that separate process: EVENT
and REQ going out, OK and EVENT coming back.

23
00:01:52,716 --> 00:01:55,887
Every acknowledgement matches the sandbox
prediction.

24
00:01:55,987 --> 00:02:02,494
Under Quiet, eleven events are admitted, and
a fresh subscriber snapshot returns seven stored records.

25
00:02:02,594 --> 00:02:06,075
Replacements and an ephemeral event explain the
difference.

26
00:02:09,657 --> 00:02:13,117
This note's author later asks the relay to
withdraw it.

27
00:02:13,217 --> 00:02:17,498
It is removed locally, and the deletion request
stays as a tombstone.

28
00:02:17,598 --> 00:02:21,324
When someone else tries to erase a note, the
request is rejected.

29
00:02:21,424 --> 00:02:25,564
The ephemeral signal reached live subscribers,
but was never stored.

30
00:02:25,664 --> 00:02:30,455
None of this promises erasure from other relays,
or from readers who kept a copy.

31
00:02:33,659 --> 00:02:40,763
Everything exports as one evidence file: inputs, arrival
times, policy and outcomes, with no signing keys.

32
00:02:40,863 --> 00:02:44,844
Importing it checks the digest and reruns every
decision.

33
00:02:48,161 --> 00:02:50,571
The same file verifies from the command line.

34
00:02:50,671 --> 00:02:58,622
The test suite covers the official BIP-340 vectors,
independent hashing, forged evidence, and a real WebSocket exchange.

35
00:02:58,722 --> 00:03:00,908
All twenty-one tests pass.

36
00:03:01,008 --> 00:03:07,752
A digest is not an outside attestation, but replay
shows that the stated outputs follow from the stated inputs.

37
00:03:11,163 --> 00:03:16,861
QuietRelay is a usable policy lab, with a
bounded local relay and reproducible tests.

38
00:03:16,961 --> 00:03:22,566
It does not detect every kind of private
information, or implement every Nostr extension.

39
00:03:22,666 --> 00:03:27,148
No wallet, no inference API, and no upstream
publication.

40
00:03:27,248 --> 00:03:29,778
Just a clear view of what gets through.
